(ii) Prior to the entry of an order for a subpoena to obtain the privileged records, the court shall
\par consider the rights of the privilege holder in such privileged records, including an appropriate means of notice to the privilege holder or holders or whether any objection to production may be resolved by redaction.
\par 
\par (ii) If a subpoena for privileged records does not include a signed authorization or court order
\par permitting the privileged records to be produced by means of subpoena, the subpoenaed person shall not appear to testify and shall not disclose any of the privileged records to the party who issued the subpoena. 
\par 
\par (C) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Objections}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . Any party or the person subpoenaed to produce records or tangible things may
\par  submit to the party issuing the subpoena a written objection to inspecting, copying, testing or sampling any or all of the materials. The objection must be submitted before the earlier of the time specified for compliance or 14 days after the subpoena is
 served. If objection is made, the party issuing the subpoena shall promptly serve a copy of the objection on all other parties. If an objection is made, the party issuing the subpoena is not entitled to inspect, copy test or sample the materials except p
ur
suant to an order of the court from which the subpoena was issued. If an objection is made, at any time on notice to the subpoenaed person and the other parties, the party issuing the subpoena may move the issuing court for an order compelling production.

