\par (3) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Quashing or Modifying a Subpoena.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
\par (A) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 When Required}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . On motion made promptly and in any event at or before the time specified in
\par  the subpoena for compliance, the issuing court must quash or modify a subpoena that:
\par 
\par (i) fails to allow a reasonable time to comply;
\par 
\par (ii) requires a person who is neither a party nor a party\rquote s officer to attend a deposition in any
\par county other than where the person resides or is employed or transacts his business in person. or at such other convenient place as is fixed by an order of court;
\par (iii) requires disclosure of privileged or other protected matter, if no exception or waiver applies; or
\par 
\par (iv) subjects a person to undue burden.
\par 
\par (B) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 When Permitted}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . To protect a person subject to or affected by a subpoena, the issuing court
\par may, on motion made promptly and in any event at or before the time specified in the subpoena for compliance, quash or modify the subpoena if it requires:
\par 
\par (i) disclosing a trade secret or other confidential research, development, or commercial
\par information; or 
\par 
\par (ii) disclosing an unretained expert\rquote s opinion or information that does not describe specific matters
\par in dispute and results from the expert\rquote s study that was not requested by a party.
\par 
\par (C) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Specifying Conditions as an Alternative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . In the circumstances described in Rule 45(c)(3)(B),
\par the court may, instead of quashing or modifying a subpoena, order attendance or production under specified conditions if the issuing party:
\par 
\par (i) shows a substantial need for the testimony or material that cannot be otherwise met without
\par undue hardship; and 
\par 
\par (ii) ensures that the subpoenaed person will be reasonably compensated.
\par 
