\par (A) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Attendance Not Required}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 .}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
 A person commanded to produce records or tangible things need not attend in person at the place of production unless also commanded to attend for a deposition, hearing, or trial.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2380224 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid2380224 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 (B) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
For Production of Privileged Records}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 .
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
\par (i) If a subpoena commands production of records from a person who provides services subject to
\par one of the privileges established by C.R.S. \'a7 13-90-107.or from the records custodian for that person, which records pertain to services performed by or at the direction of that person (\'93privileged records\'94
), such a subpoena must be accompanied by an authorization signed by the privilege holder or holders or by a court order authorizing production of such records.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2380224 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li720\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid2380224 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
(ii) Prior to the entry of an order for a subpoena to obtain the privileged records, the court shall
\par consider the rights of the privilege holder in such privileged records, including an appropriate means of notice to the privilege holder or holders or whether any objection to production may be resolved by redaction.
\par 
\par (ii) If a subpoena for privileged records does not include a signed authorization or court order
\par permitting the privileged records to be produced by means of subpoena, the subpoenaed person shall not appear to testify and shall not disclose any of the privileged records to the party who issued the subpoena. 
\par 
\par (C) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Objections}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . Any party or the person subpoenaed to produce records or tangible things may
\par  submit to the party issuing the subpoena a written objection to inspecting, copying, testing or sampling any or all of the materials. The objection must be submitted before the earlier of the time specified for compliance or 14 days after the subpoena is
 served. If objection is made, the party issuing the subpoena shall promptly serve a copy of the objection on all other parties. If an objection is made, the party issuing the subpoena is not entitled to inspect, copy test or sample the materials except p
ur
suant to an order of the court from which the subpoena was issued. If an objection is made, at any time on notice to the subpoenaed person and the other parties, the party issuing the subpoena may move the issuing court for an order compelling production.

\par 
\par (3) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Quashing or Modifying a Subpoena.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
\par (A) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 When Required}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . On motion made promptly and in any event at or before the time specified in
\par  the subpoena for compliance, the issuing court must quash or modify a subpoena that:
\par 
\par (i) fails to allow a reasonable time to comply;
\par 
\par (ii) requires a person who is neither a party nor a party\rquote s officer to attend a deposition in any
\par county other than where the person resides or is employed or transacts his business in person. or at such other convenient place as is fixed by an order of court;
\par (iii) requires disclosure of privileged or other protected matter, if no exception or waiver applies; or
\par 
\par (iv) subjects a person to undue burden.
\par 
\par (B) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 When Permitted}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . To protect a person subject to or affected by a subpoena, the issuing court
\par may, on motion made promptly and in any event at or before the time specified in the subpoena for compliance, quash or modify the subpoena if it requires:
\par 
\par (i) disclosing a trade secret or other confidential research, development, or commercial
\par information; or 
\par 
\par (ii) disclosing an unretained expert\rquote s opinion or information that does not describe specific matters
\par in dispute and results from the expert\rquote s study that was not requested by a party.
\par 
\par (C) }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Specifying Conditions as an Alternative}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 . In the circumstances described in Rule 45(c)(3)(B),
\par the court may, instead of quashing or modifying a subpoena, order attendance or production under specified conditions if the issuing party:
\par 
\par (i) shows a substantial need for the testimony or material that cannot be otherwise met without
\par undue hardship; and 
\par 
\par (ii) ensures that the subpoenaed person will be reasonably compensated.
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2380224 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 Duties in Responding to Subpoena}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid2380224\charrsid2380224 
